WEBVTT

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.520
What is that?

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:07.990
I've never seen one before.

00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:09.580
It's a musk deer.

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:11.990
The Ainu in Karafuto call it an opokay.

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:14.540
Those fangs mean it's a male.

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:22.850
Are they supposed to taste good?

00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:27.500
No, the meat's not very good, 
and their pelts aren't worth much.

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:29.600
But the males have something 
called a musk gland

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:32.800
between their navel and genitals 
that secretes a liquid...

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:34.570
Want to smell it?

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:38.390
That's awful!

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:40.730
It's like pee and Aca's armpits!

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:49.800
Once it's been dried out, 
it becomes a medicine called musk.

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:54.200
And if you water it down, 
it's supposed to attract the opposite sex.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:59.260
Not that I've ever needed help 
when it comes to getting women.

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:02.160
Wow! Your whole body is musky!

00:01:02.810 --> 00:01:05.890
Since the animals don't keep 
to a particular territory,

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:09.370
in Karafuto they call migratory 
workers "musk deer."

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:14.270
Wilk and I wandered around a lot when we 
were younger, so they called us that, too.

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:15.580
Really?

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:20.350
Come to think of it, he mentioned 
his first hunt was a musk deer, too.

00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:23.140
He cut his hohchiri off after it was over.

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:24.790
What's a hohchiri?

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:28.520
A little triangular ornament 
made of glass beads.

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:31.320
Karafuto Ainu boys put them on their bangs.

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:34.630
And when when they make their first 
kill on their own, they cut it off.

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:38.990
Asirpa, I used to wear this.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.950
When you get a little older,
 let's go hunting.

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:45.090
Until then, keep it tied to your bangs.

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:48.630
Then that was a hohchiri...

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:51.060
I didn't know it was meant for boys.

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:55.520
I've remembered something about 
Aca thanks to the musk deer.

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:57.610
I see.

00:01:58.650 --> 00:01:59.740
That's a good thing.

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:28.770
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:39.000
<b>Toyohara</b>

00:03:33.710 --> 00:03:37.160
<i>Toyohara, known today as Yuzhno-Sakhalinsk.</i>

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:41.400
<i>At the time it was the political, economic, 
and cultural center of Karafuto.</i>

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:44.110
I know you like that thing 
because Enonoka gave it to you,

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:46.490
but you're not gonna be a real 
man until you take it off.

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:49.030
I know!

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:50.520
Get back here, damn it!

00:03:51.370 --> 00:03:57.440
<b>Episode Twenty-Eight
The Immortal Sugimoto Harakiri Show</b>

00:03:51.890 --> 00:03:54.000
Somebody grab that kid!

00:03:56.150 --> 00:04:00.370
And the copy of Gansoku Maiharu's 
tattoo is in that bag?

00:04:00.370 --> 00:04:01.550
That's right!

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:35.790
<b>Yamada Circus</b>

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:39.300
Chokichi!

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:46.180
We're still not set up yet! 
Were the hell have you been?!

00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:50.160
Where'd you get that bag, boy?

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:52.970
Wait, were you at it again?

00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:55.890
That was a gun!

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:03.780
You thought that you got away, didn't you?

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:07.590
That's crazy... no one's ever been 
able to catch up to me before.

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:11.000
I am so terribly sorry!

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:14.710
I can't believe he would steal from soldiers!

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:17.110
The boy's an orphan, and wasn't raised right.

00:05:17.110 --> 00:05:20.380
I keep punishing him, but the bad 
habits just don't seem to go away!

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:23.130
Look, it's fine. We don't want 
to make a big deal out of it.

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:27.700
I can't allow him to keep being 
a menace to other people!

00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:31.910
Right here, right now, I'll have him 
take responsibility for his actions!

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:36.940
What the hell are you doing?!

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:37.850
He's just a kid!

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:39.550
Keep pressure on the cut.

00:05:39.550 --> 00:05:40.480
I'll get you to a doctor.

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:43.780
Wait... he's not even cut.

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:45.580
Was that fake blood?

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:48.760
Mine's real, though!

00:05:50.480 --> 00:05:54.160
I apologize for the shock. I was trying 
to lighten the mood a little.

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:58.120
It's called sleight of hand, you see. 
The sword has a little trick added to it.

00:05:58.570 --> 00:06:03.090
It's a tool that we used in our overseas tour,
for our big "harakiri" performance.

00:06:03.370 --> 00:06:05.420
You guys are performers, then?

00:06:05.420 --> 00:06:09.550
The lad here is Chokichi, our star acrobat.

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:12.300
An acrobat? Well, that explains it.

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:16.850
Welcome to the Yamada Circus! 
I'm the ringmaster, Yamada!

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:21.730
We've just returned to Japan after 
our acclaimed tour of Russia!

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:24.850
And we'll be putting on 
a show here in Karafuto.

00:06:24.850 --> 00:06:25.820
This is it!

00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:26.810
What is?

00:06:27.550 --> 00:06:32.410
From what the people who spotted her said, 
Asirpa can't be that far ahead of us!

00:06:33.220 --> 00:06:35.490
Put me in your Karafuto show!

00:06:35.770 --> 00:06:38.320
When the Immortal Sugimoto 
does your harakiri show,

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:41.490
everyone in Toyohara will 
be talking about it!

00:06:41.490 --> 00:06:44.330
Now, hold on! This is a bit sudden!

00:06:44.330 --> 00:06:49.430
Not to mention, I'd have to explain 
how to do the trick to you...

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:52.140
Listen, I'm no entertainer.

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:53.930
I'll take your secret to the grave.

00:06:53.930 --> 00:06:55.590
So it's no problem, right?

00:06:55.590 --> 00:06:57.520
But...

00:06:57.520 --> 00:07:00.970
I think it'd be fine, as long 
as the others join the show, too.

00:07:01.430 --> 00:07:03.540
We do have a few members 
of the troupe missing.

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:04.190
What?

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:06.190
Especially this gentlemen.

00:07:06.190 --> 00:07:09.690
I'm pretty sure you're a 
perfect fit for our world.

00:07:11.050 --> 00:07:12.490
Goodness gracious!

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:19.620
What athleticism!

00:07:20.060 --> 00:07:21.830
I was right about him.

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:26.750
Cikapasi, get back! It's dangerous!

00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:29.060
Do not let go, Sergeant Tsukishima!

00:07:29.060 --> 00:07:30.340
You had better not let go!

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:32.340
You can do it, Tanigaki Nispa!

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:33.520
Get a boner!

00:07:34.110 --> 00:07:37.260
B-Boner... Boner, boner, boner—

00:07:37.550 --> 00:07:38.910
Shut the hell up!

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:45.690
Remarkable! He's a natural-born acrobat!

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:49.110
What circus troupe were you a member of?!

00:07:49.710 --> 00:07:51.570
The 7th Division of the Imperial Army!

00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:54.080
I said not to let go, damn it!

00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:55.530
Sugimoto-san!

00:07:55.920 --> 00:07:59.740
You should practice the harakiri 
show instead of acrobatics!

00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:01.090
Does it really need practice?

00:08:01.090 --> 00:08:02.850
Of course it does!

00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:06.460
And you two, since you have absolutely 
no talent for acrobatics,

00:08:07.370 --> 00:08:10.650
join the dancing girls 
as part of the side show!

00:08:13.140 --> 00:08:16.680
Come on already, Genjiro, 
your hands are slacking again.

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:19.090
You're focusing too much on your footwork.

00:08:19.090 --> 00:08:20.140
Sorry, ma'am.

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:24.240
Are those hands only good 
for playing with your dick?

00:08:24.240 --> 00:08:25.500
No, ma'am.

00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:27.150
What're you staring at, boy?

00:08:27.450 --> 00:08:29.010
You in love with me?

00:08:29.010 --> 00:08:29.630
No.

00:08:29.630 --> 00:08:32.600
You think you'll get special treatment 
if you jump in bed with me?!

00:08:32.600 --> 00:08:33.150
No.

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:35.160
Because I don't go in for that sort of thing!

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:35.860
Okay.

00:08:39.330 --> 00:08:41.360
Magnificent!

00:08:41.900 --> 00:08:45.200
It's not just his talent, 
he looks like a star, too!

00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:48.590
Everyone in Karafuto's going 
to be talking about him!

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:50.410
Hey, enough already!

00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:52.570
If people are talking about you, 
it'll defeat the whole point!

00:08:52.570 --> 00:08:53.980
Is this jealousy?

00:08:53.980 --> 00:08:55.800
How pitiful you are, Sugimoto Saichi!

00:08:56.070 --> 00:08:57.760
No, you dumbass!

00:09:00.310 --> 00:09:02.680
We're doing this so they'll 
put Sugimoto in the show.

00:09:03.250 --> 00:09:05.110
I know it's irritating to get called slow,

00:09:05.110 --> 00:09:05.970
but you have to suck it up.

00:09:08.470 --> 00:09:13.080
If this helps us find Asirpa, 
then it'll all be worth it.

00:09:13.610 --> 00:09:17.050
I'm just... extra baggage 
for the dancing girls!

00:09:17.050 --> 00:09:19.970
I just can't dance right!

00:09:20.500 --> 00:09:22.290
I...

00:09:24.570 --> 00:09:30.250
First, you cut a sheet of paper to prove 
to the audience that the sword is real.

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:33.330
It really did cut it! Scary!

00:09:33.330 --> 00:09:35.130
Isn't using a real sword kind of dangerous?!

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:38.540
It's perfectly safe! 
That's where the gimmick comes in.

00:09:38.540 --> 00:09:40.590
Now we pray...

00:09:42.920 --> 00:09:44.600
Do I really have to?

00:09:45.360 --> 00:09:48.400
Next, we splash a bit of water,
 for purification.

00:09:48.720 --> 00:09:51.280
Is that really necessary? 
It's just a trick, right?

00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:53.400
It's absolutely crucial.

00:09:53.660 --> 00:09:56.190
Now, I'll make the cut...

00:09:58.650 --> 00:10:00.660
That makes my balls shrivel!

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:02.650
How come, Sugimoto Nispa?!

00:10:02.650 --> 00:10:03.910
No clue.

00:10:04.430 --> 00:10:07.880
And after splashing a bit 
on the leg, you cut it, too.

00:10:08.760 --> 00:10:13.300
At this point the crowd will be pale 
as a sheet, and howling in terror.

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:15.050
And then!

00:10:15.290 --> 00:10:17.250
Those are some huge nipples!

00:10:18.310 --> 00:10:19.720
Finally...

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:24.600
Seppuku!

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:38.360
And that about covers it.

00:10:38.580 --> 00:10:41.780
Then someone comes in to cover me with 
a sheet and drag me behind the scenes,

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:43.830
and the harakiri show is complete.

00:10:46.030 --> 00:10:49.860
To explain the trick, there's a groove 
running down the tip of the blade,

00:10:49.860 --> 00:10:52.560
with red dye stuffed in it.

00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:53.610
I get it.

00:10:53.610 --> 00:10:55.840
Add the water, and it starts 
to look like blood.

00:10:55.840 --> 00:10:58.000
Ready to practice a bit?

00:11:02.310 --> 00:11:03.800
He's amazing!

00:11:04.120 --> 00:11:05.880
How incredible!

00:11:07.450 --> 00:11:10.290
Try throwing a kiss toward the audience!

00:11:10.290 --> 00:11:11.880
How do you throw a kiss?

00:11:12.640 --> 00:11:14.110
Just like that!

00:11:14.110 --> 00:11:15.770
The foreign audiences loved it!

00:11:20.270 --> 00:11:21.490
Enough already!

00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:25.120
Second Lieutenant Koito! You don't 
need to be in the Karafuto show!

00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:28.290
If you've got a problem, you just need 
to outdo me with your performance!

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:33.830
Otherwise, the idea of the name Sugimoto 
becoming famous in this town is a joke!

00:11:35.820 --> 00:11:39.010
The harakiri trick gets a lot 
of attention, too, y'know.

00:11:39.010 --> 00:11:44.170
The foreign audiences were so sure I was dead,
 they wrote about it in the local news.

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:47.260
All right. I better practice.

00:11:47.610 --> 00:11:52.080
Genjiro, you're falling behind again!

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:54.360
Is that ass of yours too heavy 
for you to step lively?!

00:11:54.360 --> 00:11:55.300
Sorry, ma'am.

00:11:58.340 --> 00:12:00.150
Don't cry, Genjiro-chan.

00:12:00.510 --> 00:12:02.620
You can do it, Genjiro-chan.

00:12:02.620 --> 00:12:05.390
Come on, girls, you need to get back.

00:12:05.390 --> 00:12:07.120
Before Fumie-sensei gets mad...

00:12:07.460 --> 00:12:08.490
Okay!

00:12:08.490 --> 00:12:09.950
See you later, Genjiro-chan!

00:12:15.110 --> 00:12:20.180
Y'know, Genjiro-chan, the show 
in this town is going to be my last.

00:12:20.710 --> 00:12:22.130
Beniko-senpai?

00:12:22.950 --> 00:12:24.090
Is that true?

00:12:24.960 --> 00:12:29.810
The dancing girls are all orphans that 
the Yamada Circus looks after.

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:31.600
But once we're old enough,

00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:38.260
we get left behind when the circus 
heads to its next destination.

00:12:38.260 --> 00:12:39.430
Is that how it is?

00:12:41.510 --> 00:12:44.990
I'm so happy I get to dance with 
you in the end, Genjiro-chan.

00:12:45.770 --> 00:12:48.960
Let's make sure the Karafuto 
show is a success!

00:12:49.500 --> 00:12:50.330
Yeah!

00:12:52.330 --> 00:12:53.160
Yeah...

00:12:58.340 --> 00:13:03.720
<b>The Immortal Sugimoto Harakiri Show</b>

00:13:02.610 --> 00:13:05.690
All right, folks, we've got 
a full house tonight!

00:13:05.690 --> 00:13:08.680
Let's look sharp out there!

00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:11.240
Time to bring the curtain 
up on the Karafuto show!

00:13:12.020 --> 00:13:15.020
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:13:16.310 --> 00:13:20.540
Your attention, please!

00:13:20.540 --> 00:13:22.810
You will all be witness to the

00:13:22.810 --> 00:13:29.550
performances of the Yamada Circus, 
which have dazzled all of Russia!

00:13:29.550 --> 00:13:34.630
And now it is our honor to bring 
them here to you on this day!

00:13:37.420 --> 00:13:38.530
All right!

00:13:48.460 --> 00:13:49.800
Koito Nispa!

00:13:53.320 --> 00:13:55.110
Just you wait, Lieutenant Koito!

00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:07.560
<i>Beniko-senpai!</i>

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:15.850
And next up, Koito Otonoshin 
will cross the high wire!

00:14:16.740 --> 00:14:17.910
That's...

00:14:18.320 --> 00:14:22.040
A picture of Lieutenant Tsurumi!
 What's it doing here?!

00:14:29.850 --> 00:14:30.590
What the...

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:06.570
We have witnessed an acrobatic god!

00:15:07.890 --> 00:15:09.850
Damn you, Sugimoto!

00:15:09.850 --> 00:15:11.700
You rifled through my things,

00:15:11.700 --> 00:15:15.440
then tried to sabotage me with my 
picture of Lieutenant Tsurumi!

00:15:15.440 --> 00:15:17.470
You cold-blooded bastard!

00:15:22.590 --> 00:15:23.540
Genjiro!

00:15:28.720 --> 00:15:30.160
You looked good.

00:15:33.110 --> 00:15:35.390
<b>Yamada Circus Troupe</b>

00:15:33.590 --> 00:15:40.830
And now for our final performance, 
the Yamada Circus's big closer!

00:15:43.120 --> 00:15:47.500
The Immortal Sugimoto Harakiri show!

00:15:48.460 --> 00:15:50.040
<i>This needs to reach Asirpa-san.</i>

00:15:50.450 --> 00:15:51.740
<i>I'm still alive!</i>

00:15:53.170 --> 00:15:54.620
What's going on here?

00:15:54.620 --> 00:15:56.300
There are two of this picture?

00:15:57.060 --> 00:15:58.410
Wait, it's slightly different!

00:15:58.410 --> 00:16:01.290
Sugimoto wouldn't have a picture like this...

00:16:01.290 --> 00:16:03.020
I was the one who did it.

00:16:03.850 --> 00:16:05.480
Tsukishima?!

00:16:05.800 --> 00:16:09.580
Any way you think about it, you were 
standing out more, Lieutenant Koito.

00:16:10.010 --> 00:16:12.700
That defeats the whole 
point of the performance.

00:16:13.530 --> 00:16:17.410
I thought some sabotage 
would solve the problem.

00:16:17.780 --> 00:16:19.150
This is bad.

00:16:19.150 --> 00:16:20.440
What's wrong?

00:16:20.870 --> 00:16:25.080
I replaced that katana's blade 
with my own, for payback.

00:16:26.790 --> 00:16:28.750
Oh, so, so cold!

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:32.050
You don't have to sell them 
on how cold the water is!

00:16:35.990 --> 00:16:37.820
I'm gonna cut my arm!

00:16:37.820 --> 00:16:40.940
Here goes!

00:16:46.980 --> 00:16:50.720
I'm gonna cut it! Here I go!

00:16:53.150 --> 00:16:54.560
Get on with it!

00:16:54.560 --> 00:16:56.060
Cut yourself!

00:16:56.670 --> 00:16:58.640
Okay, here I go!

00:17:06.480 --> 00:17:07.570
The blood...

00:17:06.860 --> 00:17:09.250
Er... that actually hurt.

00:17:10.020 --> 00:17:11.460
<i>I'm actually cut.</i>

00:17:19.060 --> 00:17:20.540
<i>This is a real sword!</i>

00:17:21.610 --> 00:17:23.660
<i>Now what? Should I cut the act short?</i>

00:17:23.660 --> 00:17:25.220
<i>Swap the swords out?</i>

00:17:25.850 --> 00:17:29.930
<i>No, it'd stand out too much! 
The crowd would definitely lose interest!</i>

00:17:37.940 --> 00:17:39.370
He's going to keep going?!

00:17:39.770 --> 00:17:43.280
I can't back down in front 
of a huge crowd like this!

00:17:44.130 --> 00:17:46.220
That blood looks real!

00:17:46.220 --> 00:17:47.620
'Cuz it is!

00:17:52.430 --> 00:17:56.380
<i>Have to be careful... not to 
hit anything important...</i>

00:17:56.780 --> 00:17:58.430
<i>This is all...</i>

00:17:59.060 --> 00:18:00.470
<i>To find Asirpa-san!</i>

00:18:10.460 --> 00:18:12.570
Who are those Russians?

00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:29.810
What a trick!

00:18:29.810 --> 00:18:31.580
It looks so real!

00:18:35.610 --> 00:18:38.930
Get out there and bow for the crowd! 
And grab the bodies while they're distracted!

00:18:38.930 --> 00:18:40.010
Okay!

00:18:54.420 --> 00:18:57.150
Seems their actual target
 was the ringmaster...

00:18:57.690 --> 00:19:01.990
Since their orders were to go after the 
man performing the harakiri show.

00:19:02.300 --> 00:19:06.070
But this was the one time that 
just happened to be Sugimoto.

00:19:06.070 --> 00:19:07.200
Who hired them?

00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:10.000
Someone from the 
Russian government, they said.

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:12.680
Why would the Russians 
be after the ringmaster?

00:19:14.210 --> 00:19:16.380
You're a spy, aren't you?

00:19:19.030 --> 00:19:23.250
That's right. I was originally an 
officer with the Imperial Army.

00:19:23.250 --> 00:19:28.110
I was embedded in Russia for 
years before the war broke out,

00:19:28.110 --> 00:19:31.190
where I acted as an intelligence 
operative behind the scenes.

00:19:31.650 --> 00:19:35.310
The Russian government 
probably caught onto my identity.

00:19:37.050 --> 00:19:38.360
Bloody hell...

00:19:41.300 --> 00:19:43.200
Well, you're one shitty spy.

00:19:49.270 --> 00:19:54.500
Bury all three of them under the tent. 
We'll be pulling out in the morning, too.

00:19:55.130 --> 00:19:57.550
This place was just an empty field, anyway.

00:20:01.560 --> 00:20:03.010
Take care of yourselves, okay?

00:20:03.380 --> 00:20:05.080
Beniko-senpai...

00:20:05.770 --> 00:20:10.230
Genjiro-chan! Don't forget 
about me or the girls, okay?

00:20:11.430 --> 00:20:12.330
Yeah!

00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:16.020
There's a write-up about 
the show in the paper.

00:20:16.230 --> 00:20:17.310
There is?!

00:20:17.310 --> 00:20:18.860
What's it say about me?

00:20:19.120 --> 00:20:20.910
It's got about...

00:20:20.910 --> 00:20:22.280
Two sentences.

00:20:22.280 --> 00:20:23.320
And it's a misprint!

00:20:22.320 --> 00:20:23.320
<b>The Immoral Sugimoto</b>

00:20:23.320 --> 00:20:25.530
Damn it all!

00:20:25.780 --> 00:20:27.150
Koito-kun!

00:20:27.150 --> 00:20:29.740
We plan on traveling to America some day!

00:20:29.740 --> 00:20:32.290
With your acrobatics, you could have 
the world eating out of your hand!

00:20:32.290 --> 00:20:35.080
Please, join the Yamada Circus!

00:20:35.080 --> 00:20:36.330
I can't do that.

00:20:36.330 --> 00:20:37.920
Why?!

00:20:37.920 --> 00:20:40.560
Because Lieutenant Tsurumi wouldn't like it.

00:20:42.580 --> 00:20:44.970
We're looking for some people.

00:20:45.260 --> 00:20:49.220
One of them is a part of a partisan group 
that's made up of a ethnic minority

00:20:49.220 --> 00:20:50.680
from the Amur River area.

00:20:50.680 --> 00:20:54.340
We believe he's headed north to 
rendezvous with his comrades.

00:20:54.810 --> 00:20:56.720
Do you know anything that might help?

00:20:56.720 --> 00:20:58.170
Partisans?

00:20:58.980 --> 00:21:01.650
One thing comes to mind.

00:21:02.290 --> 00:21:07.600
About 530 kilometers north of Toyohara,
 in a Russian port town,

00:21:07.600 --> 00:21:12.640
there's the biggest prison 
in Karafuto, Alexandrovskaya Prison.

00:21:13.210 --> 00:21:18.110
I heard a large group of eastern minorities

00:21:18.110 --> 00:21:21.250
was moved there for plotting a resistance.

00:21:22.060 --> 00:21:26.430
That definitely sounds like 
where Kiroranke would be headed.

00:21:27.450 --> 00:21:30.040
The performance might not have helped,

00:21:30.040 --> 00:21:33.200
but we got some important 
intel from Ringmaster Yamada.

00:21:33.200 --> 00:21:35.020
It did help.

00:21:35.020 --> 00:21:37.840
It might only be two sentences, 
and there's a misprint,

00:21:37.840 --> 00:21:41.020
but Asirpa-san is sharp enough 
to understand, if she reads it.

00:21:41.460 --> 00:21:45.710
I just hope those beautiful blue 
eyes are catching a glimpse

00:21:45.710 --> 00:21:48.030
of the proof that I'm alive.

00:21:48.740 --> 00:21:51.170
Hey, Shiraishi, look at this.

00:21:51.910 --> 00:21:54.490
It's poop! And it's still steaming!

00:21:54.490 --> 00:21:56.870
That means there there must 
be some big game in the area!

00:21:57.230 --> 00:22:00.410
That's my poop from a few minutes ago.

00:22:00.410 --> 00:22:04.550
<i>Asirpa was catching a glimpse 
of Shiraishi's turd.</i>

00:23:35.320 --> 00:23:40.250
<b>Next Time
The Border</b>

00:23:36.660 --> 00:23:40.020
Next Time: "The Border."
